      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Pellucid Grotto [zone=707]\n**Who:**\n- Tronten the Subnexus [npc=34211]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Spell\n**Quest Items:**\n- Big Grey Bag of Complaints [item=86623]\n- Gem of Destruction [item=86547]\n- Gem of Life [item=86541]\n- Gem of Pain [item=86445]\n- Gem of Resilience [item=86483]\n- Gem of Structure [item=86539]\n- Refined Seeding Gem [item=86538]\n- Voskatik's Message Jelly [item=86551]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Pellucid Grotto: Seeding Frenzy [zone=718]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Bammor the Magnite [npc=34558]\n- Cheon the Workmaster [npc=34567]\n- Geltior the Gembringer [npc=34560]\n- General Voskatik [npc=34572]\n- Oduz the Magnite [npc=34559]\n- a cliknar scalder [npc=34571]\n- a cliknar thrasher [npc=34569]\n- a cliknar vexer [npc=34570]\n- a crustal seeder [npc=34563]\n- a rebellious gembringer [npc=34564]\n- a rebellious gemcracker [npc=34568]\n- a rebellious gempolisher [npc=34565]\n- a rebellious gemstacker [npc=34566]\n- an unadorned chest [npc=35238]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Filling the Repository [quest=4908]\n- Gem Collector [quest=6740]\n- Kronk Kollus #1: A Many-Faceted Dilemma [quest=4907]\n- Kronk Kollus #2: A Delicate Matter [quest=4927]\n- Seeding Frenzy Challenge of Toughness [quest=6739]\n- Seeding Frenzy Time Trial [quest=6738]\n**Era:** | !Underfoot\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Dec 15 03:20:03 2009\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This is a group task (3-6 players) that begins with Tronten the Subnexus in Pellucid Grotto, location: +345, 360, 15._\n_In order to request this task, you must first have completed pre-requisite tasks: \"A Many Faceted Dilemma\", \"A Delicate Matter\", and \"Filling the Repository\"._\nYou say, 'Hail, Tronten the Subnexus'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Mortals of flesh. I must suffer them. I must use them to maintain control in the Repository. I must have their [help].'\nYou say, 'How can we help?'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'From the moment time came to this place, until very near to now, all have known the presence of Brell Serilis, our creator. Now he is not present. This distresses us all. Never has there been time passing in Underfoot without him being near. Never until now. I suffer much confusion. We all suffer. Some now question their purpose, to [dangerous] [effects].'\nYou say, 'Dangerous?'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Aggression from the Autarchian have made production very slow. They constantly get in the way and impede our progress, and I feel it is time someone does the [same] to them.'\nYou say, 'What effects'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Yes. All of us ask questions. Some ask questions that cannot be answered. Some take the lack of answers to be a loss of purpose. Some come to the conclusion that because change has come to the Underfoot without explanation, certain things that have always been done need no longer be done. Some have put down the duties that have driven them for most of eternity. This is dangerous. They were created by Brell to do what they must. They cannot change. . . they must not [change].'\nYou say, 'Change?'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'I see no reason for these awkward differences of thought to appear. Yet they have, and now that there are differences of thinking, the owners of those thoughts refuse to change them. I am disturbed by this. We learned a new word from you mortals who now come to visit us. . . [faction].'\nYou say, 'Faction...'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'The disunity of thought, and the factions among us which have been created by this phenomenon, threaten to destroy this place. All of the Pellucid Grotto is threatened. I understand it not. Those who agree with Tronten remain followers of Brell, though some doubt he will ever return. Those who disagree with Tronten are mostly followers of the Church of Self, who teaches them to abandon their duties and do whatever pleases them. Then there are the [Cliknar] who follow none but the whims of their hive-mind. Gem [production] and distribution has slowed dangerously since this disunity began. I am very frustrated by this.'\nYou say, 'Gem production?'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'We are the ones who mine, fashion, and polish the gems, crystals, and lesser minerals, which are placed into your mortal worlds. Were our duties to cease, not only would the supply of precious gems come to a halt, but your worlds would erode, the mana would ebb away, the lines of magic would unbind everywhere, and the waking worlds would start to die. All things are touched by what we make for the [Repository]. You should be concerned about this.'\nYou say, 'The repository?'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'The Repository is breaking down. Loyalists and rebels among the crystalkin continually stop doing their duty, and descend into pointless arguments over belief systems. Even more distastefully, these arguments often descend further until violence happens. [Will] you help us bring stability to the Repository?'\nYou say, 'We will'\n_Without pre-requisites:_\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Flesh being must prove worthiness and skill. Must earn trust of Magnite Ordinator Bammor and Kut'Kollus before being given important task.\n_With pre-requisites:_\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Please go and speak with Bammor, leader of the Magnite Golems. These Magnites have served Brell's will in the Repository since he first created it. Bammor knows what needs to be done. If you assist him, there will be materials I could offer as rewards. I would thank you. I am pleased you are helping us. Tell me when you are ready to [go] to the Repository on this mission.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Seeding Frenzy'.\nTronten the Subnexus is aware of breakdowns in gem production occurring in the Grotto, which he finds unaccpetable. The gems must flow! Whatever is threatening the safety of the Repository enough that Bammor would send Tronten a message of distress must be dealt with at once!\n_To zone in:_\nYou say, 'Ready to go!'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Practice caution in all you do. These are difficult times for the Underfoot.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Pellucid Grotto - Seeding Frenzy.\n\n---\n\n_The first five steps take place in the Magnite temple (western part of the zone; same place as Kronk in non-instance Pellucid)._\nSpeak with Bammor the Magnite 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Bammor the Magnite'\nBammor the Magnite says 'So, Tronten has at last sent us agents who will help rectify our labor shortages and defend this repository. With all the problems recently -- the crystalkin rebelling and the cliknar attacking -- we could use the help. Please begin your work by conferring with Oduz and Geltior. They will explain how the magnites are afflicted by the schism among the crystalkin and the schemes of the cliknar.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nSpeak with Oduz the Magnite 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Oduz the Magnite'\nOduz the Magnite says 'We magnites labor endlessly to fill the worlds of all creation with the gems needed to keep their mana flowing and economies rich. We rely on the labors of the crystalkin to provide us with finished gems to seed into the worlds. Without their help, we quickly become useless. Nearly half the crystalkin now fail to heed the words of Brell. Without the gems they are supposed to bring us, your world, Norrath, will soon falter and wither. They must be encouraged to assist us. I fear there is no workable solution as long as they insist upon disagreement and resistance to the way of Brell.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nSpeak with Geltior the Gembringer 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Geltior the Gembringer'\nGeltior the Gembringer says 'I have nothing but complaints regarding the way things have been run in the Repository since Brell disappeared. I almost think some of the autarchian crystalkin might have been right about the breakdowns that have been occurring. They think we should reason with the cliknar, give them a percentage of gems in exchance for peace. It would be better than the constant attacks we have been facing. Here, take this bag of complaint forms to Bammor. Maybe after reading these he'll reconsider his positions and put things in working order.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nDeliver Big Grey Bag of Complaints to Bammor 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nBammor the Magnite says 'It appears the other gembringers and magnites are allowing their fears and doubts to subvert their better judgment. Let it be known that Geltior's lengthy list of complaints will not return Brell Serilis to the Underfoot from wherever it is he has gone, nor will it add progress to the duties set before us by Brell himself. We must prevail upon the Autarchians to return to their senses and once again aid our efforts in the Repository. And we must never try to reason with the insidious hive mind of the cliknar.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nSpeak with Bammor 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Bammor the Magnite'\nBammor the Magnite says 'We can only solve the dilemma one step at a time. Before facing the cliknar, our front should be united. You will take my order to Cheon the Workmaster, who huddles with his autarchian cronies near the Black Plinth to the east of Geodech, in defiance of Brell's will. Cheon must submit at once and resume his duties. If he does not comply, be prepared to convince him to do so by force. Regardless of his choice, I will need the gems his workers are carrying. The work must continue; the seeders must have the gems.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Cheon 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\n_Through a tunnel to the immediate east of the port-in point, you will come out into an opening full of rebellious crystalkin and a named, Cheon the Workmaster. Mobs become aggro as you hail Cheon, it's generally best for one person to do the hail while the rest wait in the tunnel and use that as a pull point._\nYou say, 'Hail, Cheon the Workmaster'\nCheon the Workmaster says 'Of course we will not submit to Bammor's order. We serve our own will now. We have awakened to the truth of the Way of Self, and will aspire to serve our Autarchy in the pursuit of goals that are more meaningful than doing Brell's will. It is past time for Bammor to accept that the old ways are done. Brell has forsaken us. As well, we forsake those who strive to keep us to a fruitless path. You are an agent of Bammor; you are to be eliminated.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nCheon the Workmaster says 'I will grind you into dust!'\nDestroy the rebellious crystalkin 0/18 (Pellucid Grotto)\nDestroy Cheon 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\n_Task Window Says:_ Negotiations have broken down. Kill the rebellious crystalkin warriors and eliminate Cheon; his irredeemable stance is only going to get more crystalkin killed.\n_Cheon hits for a max ~8,000; AE rampages; and single-target rampages while the rebellious crystalkin (which can each be pulled single or mezzed) hit for a max ~6,000._\n_Be sure to loot the Refined Seeding Gems from the crystalkin. You need 20 of them._\n_After the above kill steps and looted items are done, everyone should move to the magnite temple before completing the next series of hails, after which 15 cliknar + 1 named spawn on the bridge._\n\n---\n\nDeliver the rebels' gems to the crustal seeder 0/20 (Pellucid Grotto)\n_The crustal seeder is in the same room with Bammor, Geltior, and other quest NPCs._\nSpeak with Bammor 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Bammor the Magnite'\nBammor the Magnite says 'Unfortunate that the rebellious autarchians made resistance. Their deaths are regrettable, but at least the gems they carried have been given to the crustal seeders. I will send word to Tronten to organize a new work team. Now, to deal with the cliknar threat. They have been attacking the workers and stealing our gems. Geltior knows more about the threat. Speak with him.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nSpeak with Geltior about the Cliknar threat 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Geltior the Gembringer'\nGeltior the Gembringer says 'Bammor is still worried about the cliknar attacks? Yes, they have been bothering us, but I think I found a solution. I spoke to one of them, Voskatik, and I think I have secured the peace. He will stay away from the Repository as long as...wait, I hear clicking coming from outside...'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\n_16 cliknar (including a named) spawn outside the room you're in, on the bridge over the lava. They can be single-pulled. The non-named cliknar hit for a max ~6,500 and summon. They are stunnable and mezzable. The 85th level cliknar are rootable/snareable while the higher level ones are not._\n_The General hits for a max ~8,000 and summons. He's immune to mez, stun, and root._\nDestroy the invading Cliknar 0/15 (Pellucid Grotto)\nDestroy Voskatik and salvage any information jelly he is carrying 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\n_NOTE: The task locks upon the General's death. Loot the \"Voskatik's Message Jelly\" from his corpse._\nDeliver the jelly to Geltior 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nGeltior the Gembringer says 'I see you have Voskatik's memory jelly. This is proof I intended no wrong! Thank you for giving me the chance to explain my conversation with the cliknar leader. I did not know he would try to attack. I told him he could have a certain percentage of our gems, in exchange for peace. I gave him ten whole sacks of gems, but I suppose that wasn't enough. I cannot believe they tried to kill us and take all of the gems! Do they not understand that creatures of Brell must not destroy each other here in the Underfoot?'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nTell Bammor that the thread has passed, for now 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nYou say, 'Hail, Bammor the Magnite'\nBammor the Magnite says 'I thank you for your assistance. I will have to have a conversation with Geltior about his folly. It almost cost us our lives -- and the lives of countless other creatures. Cliknar violating the sanctity of this place could only mean they are interested in destroying other worlds. Perhaps they would overseed worlds like Norrath below, with enough gems to cause a mana disjunction or something even worse. Stopping them was a good thing; Brell would not have been pleased to see our Repository duties ended. [Leave] me now and speak with Tronten.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nYou say, 'I wish to leave'\nBammor the Magnite says 'Tell Tronten we can always use more adventurers to protect the Repository.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Pellucid Grotto.\nSpeak with Tronten 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nReturn to Tronten the Subnexus and report your success in restoring the flow of gems to Norrath.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tronten the Subnexus'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Very well. Mortals did as I asked. Depredations of autarchian crystalkin thwarted; cliknar assault has been repulsed. There is much damage to repair, but I am pleased. May Brell return to us before more destructive events take place.'\nYour task 'The Seeding Frenzy' has been updated.\nYou have crushed the crystalkin rebellion and successfully prevented a cliknar takeover of the Magnite Repository! Had this institution fallen into cliknar hands, it would have given the cliknar the power to disrupt the manaflows of Norrath.\n_An unadorned chest spawns with loot (1 item per task). Known drops:_\nBile-Etched War Axe\nCliknar Limb Flute\nCracked Crystalkin Heart\nCrystaldust Sleeves\nCrystalglow Energy Aura\nEssence Scour\nFire-formed Obsidian Shard\nRock Guardian Shard\nShard of Pain\nShield of Coiled Terror\n_Rewards (everyone in task):_\n315 platinum\nExperience (3.3 AAs at Level 85)\n\n---\n\n_Some (not all) classes also receive a level 83 spell for completion of this mission:_\nBard - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBeastlord - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBerserker - Tome of Vigorous Axe Throw\nCleric - You'll get nothing and like it!\nDruid - Spell: Remote Manaflux\nEnchanter - You'll get nothing and like it!\nMagician - You'll get nothing and like it!\nMonk - Tome of Vigorous Shuriken\nNecromancer - Spell: Bestow Undeath\nPaladin - You'll get nothing and like it!\nRanger - You'll get nothing and like it!\nRogue - Tome of Vigorous Dagger-Throw\nShadow Knight - Spell: Unsavory Sacrifice\nShaman - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWarrior - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWizard - You'll get nothing and like it!\nThere is a side quest in here that you may complete during this task. If you collect the following, you will get 10 Achievement Points and an achievement:\nGem of Destruction\nGem of Life\nGem of Pain\nGem of Resilience\nGem of Structure\nYou have completed achievement: Gem Collector\n- Bile-Etched War Axe [item=86901]\n- Cliknar Limb Flute [item=85975]\n- Cracked Crystalkin Heart [item=86745]\n- Crystaldust Sleeves [item=86952]\n- Crystalglow Energy Aura [item=86899]\n- Essence Scour [item=87480]\n- Fire-Formed Obsidian Shard [item=86425]\n- Rock Guardian Shard [item=85936]\n- Shard of Pain [item=86747]\n- Shield of Coiled Terror [item=85968]\n- Spell: Bestow Undeath [item=86552]\n- Spell: Remote Manaflux [item=86133]\n- Spell: Unsavory Sacrifice [item=87226]\n- Tome of Vigorous Axe Throw [item=86635]\n- Tome of Vigorous Dagger-Throw [item=86540]\n- Tome of Vigorous Shuriken [item=86422]",
